carbonenginejs/format-dxbc
==========================

A pure-JavaScript reader for Microsoft DXBC (Direct3D compiled shader
bytecode) containers and the SM4/SM5 instruction token stream.

Contains no Microsoft, CarbonEngine, or Fenris Creations (CCP Games) code.
DXBC is a Microsoft format, and Microsoft publishes it:

- the SM4/SM5 instruction token encoding in `D3D12TokenizedProgramFormat.hpp`,
  part of Microsoft's DirectX-Headers, MIT License
  (<https://github.com/microsoft/DirectX-Headers>), and the matching
  d3d11TokenizedProgramFormat header in the Windows Driver Kit;
- the outer container in Microsoft's open-source DirectX Shader Compiler
  (<https://github.com/microsoft/DirectXShaderCompiler>, University of Illinois
  Open Source License) and LLVM's DXContainer documentation.

Unity Technologies' HLSLcc (MIT) was used as a behavioral reference while
auditing instruction semantics; no HLSLcc source is included in this
repository.

`CjsDxbcFormat.disassemble` prints the decoded token stream as assembly text,
as Microsoft's own shader compiler does. It applies to compiled shader files,
which are game content, and never to any application's program code.
CarbonEngine and Fenris Creations (CCP Games) are mentioned for interoperability
and target-ecosystem context only.

